  "title": "Technology stories are moving from demos into physical systems",
  "summary": "The week’s technology coverage is notably physical. China’s agricultural technology fair focuses attention on machinery and field adoption; Ukraine and JEF partners are linking defence needs to practical technology cooperation; and the Redwire discussion centres on phased-array systems rather than a consumer launch. These stories share a lesson: the commercial and strategic value of technology is increasingly decided by integration, procurement and operating conditions after the prototype stage.",
